// # Render Subsystem Anchor - Emitted Lines To Output
//
// Logline: Shapes followed lines for the terminal, honouring prefix and colouring.
//
// Setup: Skeleton. Pure text over assembled lines, shared by stdout and socket.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Prefix each line with the source file, optionally with a line number.
//   2. Emit nothing but bytes when colour is off, so IPC output stays clean.
// No implementation yet. This anchor is the documented landing zone for the
// render pages and gives `make verify` a page to check in this domain.
//
// Keep colour off unless asked, because a socket peer wants raw bytes and escape
// codes in a payload are a bug. Build an escape byte explicitly: the string
// literal does not emit one, and guessing here puts an unescaped ESC on the wire.
//
// First page to write: render_line.oo with colour disabled, which is the shape
// both stdout and a socket frame can share unchanged.
